    "updated_at": "2026-10-10T20:29:54Z",
    "body": "> However, I think this change might regress the original problem that was attempted to solve: #24746\r\n\r\nI checked #24746 with and without this change: a pinned request to an idle slot still restores from the RAM cache, and a pinned request to a busy slot now waits and restores when the slot frees up, since the deferred task goes back through get_available_slot. Measured on Qwen3-0.6B (dense), Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (hybrid) and Gemma 4 E2B (SWA), the restored token count is the same in both builds; the only difference in the logs is that the restore now happens after the defer instead of into the busy slot.",
